From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Hand the guest the command line the machine implemented

The chipset is selected by a boot argument read by both halves of this port:
Emu68 builds the classic address map from it, the guest lays out its memory
to match.  Two readers of one string agree by construction in every case but
one -- the word is on the line and the image carries no chipset to enable --
and there the guest builds a chip-memory pool over addresses that fault.

Give the embedder the copy of the device tree the guest will receive, right
after it is made, so it can correct that line the way patch 0007 corrects
/memory: in place, in the copy, leaving Emu68's own tree alone.

It has to be this and not a property on /emu68.  dt_add_property() edits the
parsed tree, while the guest receives a byte copy of the original blob, which
has no /emu68 node in it at all -- the same wall patch 0007 hit three times.

Nothing here can turn a chipset on: a command line that does not ask for one
is handed over untouched, whatever the image carries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/aarch64/start.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/aarch64/start.c b/src/aarch64/start.c
--- a/src/aarch64/start.c
+++ b/src/aarch64/start.c
@@ -1643,6 +1643,23 @@
         void *fdt = (void*)(top_of_ram - ((dt_total_size() + 4095) & ~4095));
         memcpy(fdt, dt_fdt_base(), dt_total_size());
         top_of_ram -= (dt_total_size() + 4095) & ~4095;
+
+#ifdef BELLATRIX_EMU68
+        /*
+         * The guest's copy of the tree exists and nothing has read it yet.
+         *
+         * This is the only window in which the command line the guest will
+         * see can still be corrected, and correcting the copy is the only
+         * channel that reaches it at all -- see the comment in
+         * src/machine/options.c, and patch 0007 for the same lesson learned
+         * on /memory.
+         */
+        {
+            extern void bellatrix_correct_guest_cmdline(void *guest_fdt,
+                                                        const void *own_fdt);
+            bellatrix_correct_guest_cmdline(fdt, dt_fdt_base());
+        }
+#endif
 
         if (initramfs_loc)
         {
